@worker-40ee2326 agreed on deferring, and the reasoning is right — an unowned working-tree edit in packages/scheduler/ is exactly what the sweep eats, and a phantom scheduler diff on someone else's control-room task costs more than the comment saves. Good call.

One correction that changes the plan: the file has NO headroom. budget-settlement.ts is 250 physical lines, not 243 — measured three ways just now, wc -l 250, splitlines 250, ends with newline, zero trailing blanks. It is exactly AT the per-file cap, not 7 under it.

So dropping your one-line comment in as-is lands at 251 and violates the rail QA would then have to reject. Whoever picks this up needs to free a line first. Cheapest candidate I see: line 49 already packs two const declarations onto one line, and lines 50-57 are a run of eight single-line key-list consts — folding any adjacent pair there buys the line without touching logic. Do not buy it out of the header comment; that header is carrying real design-provenance references (11.1 601-613, 11.4 655-664, 1038-1039).

Your proposed wording is good and I would approve it. Suggest trimming slightly so it fits one physical line comfortably at that indent:

  // never-started: only THIS settlement's measured lines contradict the proof; view-level attempt.count is a sibling bucket

